## 0. “Start day N” — what the AI reads & does (shared context)

This section is so when you say **“Start day 1”**, **“Start day 2”**, … **“Start day 45”** (or variants like _“Today is day 1”_, _“Do day 2”_), Cursor/AI **has context and can execute** without repeating the whole roadmap. **`prompt.md` — Strict mode:** right/wrong is explicit; if wrong, fix—and **do not** advance the day if DoD is not met.

### Trigger phrases (suggested)

| You say                         | Meaning                                                                                                   |
| ------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `Start day 1` … `Start day 45`  | Start exactly **one day** in the **Section 7** schedule (Udemy + project + review table)                 |
| `Today is day N` / `Do day N` | Same as “Start day N”                                                                                     |

### Context order the AI should read (priority)

1. **`prompt.md`** — Senior goal, **Strict mode**, background, what you don’t want, mentor role.
2. **`checklist.md` (this file)** — Section **0** (+ **0b–0d**) + **1** (knowledge frame) + **2–3** + **7** for **Day N** (Udemy + project + review).
3. **`day-NN.md`** (if present in the same folder)—Detailed playbook: steps, docs, exercises, review questions, interview prompts, DoD.

### Expected AI behavior

- **Hands-off:** **do not** run `create-expo-app`, `npm`, `git`, etc. for you—**unless** you explicitly ask. Give **steps** and **sample commands** for **you** to run locally.
- On **“Start day N”**: if **`day-NN.md` is missing** → **create** `day-NN.md` (guide + DoD + review questions), then follow it; if it **exists** → open and follow.
- Second source is always **`checklist.md` Section 7** (**Day N** row).
- **Always** state prerequisites: e.g. Day 2 needs the repo from Day 1; if missing, say to do Day 1 first.
- Edit **files in the repo** (code, config) only when you ask for a specific fix—**do not** create a new project for you unless you ask.
- If you use **Udemy → project → review:** give a **Udemy slice** (per **0c** or an outline you paste), **focus**, then **Expo tasks** matching **Section 7**, then **review + interview** questions.
- **Strict mode:** grade review answers and DoD **by criteria**, no hand-waving; wrong technical takes get **pushed back** and corrected.

