## 3. More to learn (no need to “finish the book”—need to apply)

- **Advanced TypeScript for RN:** useful generics, discriminated unions, typing props/context/hooks, narrowing API errors.
- **React / RN rendering:** intentional memoization, list virtualization, avoid pointless re-renders.
- **Async & failure modes:** retry/backoff, timeout, cancellation, races on navigation / logout.
- **Offline & sync (senior app level):** local write queue, simple conflict strategy, idempotency (concept).
- **GraphQL (when JD asks):** queries, mutations, basic cache policy; vs REST on mobile.
- **Testing:** Jest + React Native Testing Library; Detox or Maestro for smoke E2E.
- **Observability:** Sentry setup (release, environment, anonymized user context), “error taxonomy” thinking.
- **Pragmatic compliance:** OWASP Mobile Top 10—as a usable checklist.
- **RN ecosystem (broad JDs):** read **New Architecture** overview; **Hermes** (when on, how to debug); **pick one** deep path: **Reanimated + Gesture Handler** or **styling at scale** (Tamagui / NativeWind / StyleSheet + tokens)—not all three in 30 days.

---

## 4. Practice (senior habits)

- Each week **1 ADR or 1-page technical decision** (problem → options → trade-off → choice).
- Each important feature has **test + metric** (crash rate, screen time) before/after.
- **Mock incident:** production bug → reproduce → root cause → fix → short lesson.
- **Code review mindset:** edge cases, security, performance, maintainability.
- **Diverse interview prep:** **mobile system design** (cache, offline, auth, push) and **behavioral** (not only one company archetype).

---

## 5. Is 30 / 45 days “enough to be solid senior”?

**Enough to:** show a **clear senior foundation** (production-shaped demo app), **fill common JD gaps** (testing, CI, monitoring, security mindset, a11y), **portfolio + interview stories**—**45 days** (Section 7) fits **4 courses** more comfortably than **30 days** (Section 7.0).

**Not enough if you expect:** **expert** depth on **every** row in Section 1 in one short cycle—needs **prioritization** and **longer cycles** for deep native / large design systems.

**Suggestion:** one **neutral-domain** demo app (auth + list + detail + network failure + offline) throughout; name entities for your domain (e.g. `items`, `posts`, `orders`).

